# MarkUP showcase

This document uses every construct of the language. Markdown works as usual —
*emphasis*, **strong**, `code`, [links](https://github.com/arturjoaodaros-dev/MarkUP),
~~strikethrough~~ and footnotes[^footnotes] — and directives add components.

::toc[On this page]{depth=3}

## Callouts

:::note
Callouts mark information that stands apart from the text. There are five: `note`, `tip`,
`important`, `warning` and `caution`.
:::

:::tip[Keyboard]
Press :kbd[Ctrl+Shift+P] in MarkUP Desktop to open the command palette.
:::

:::warning{collapsible}
A collapsible callout. The body is hidden until the reader opens it.
:::

## Layout

::::columns
:::column
:::card[Parser]
`@markup-lang/core` reads blocks, inlines, directives and data into a syntax tree with positions.
:::
:::
:::column
:::card[Renderers]
`@markup-lang/html` and `@markup-lang/text` turn the tree into HTML or plain text.
:::
:::
:::column
:::card[Editors]
The language service gives VS Code and MarkUP Desktop the same completion and diagnostics.
:::
:::
::::

::::tabs
:::tab[Build from source]
```sh
git clone https://github.com/arturjoaodaros-dev/MarkUP
cd MarkUP && npm install && npm run build
```
:::
:::tab[Run the CLI]
```sh
node packages/cli/dist/markup.js build examples --out site
```
:::
::::

