## Text

> A block quote. It can contain any block, including components.

1. Write the document in any editor.
2. Check it with `markup check`.
3. Build it with `markup build`.

- [x] Windows installer
- [ ] macOS and Linux packages

:::details[Why is there no raw HTML?]
`<div>` is shown as text. Documents stay independent of the output format, and previews
are safe. Use components, and :abbr[CSS]{title="Cascading Style Sheets"} classes on them, instead.
:::

```ts {title="render.ts"}
import { markupToHtml } from '@markup-lang/html';

const { html, diagnostics } = markupToHtml('# Hello');
```

[^footnotes]: Footnotes are collected at the end of the document, with links back to each reference.
